+  are skipped. A bad row answers `bad_request`, an item running out answers
+  `sale_out_of_stock` (409); either way the message names the row (`row 2`
+  is the first data row) and nothing from the file is imported.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers one line per
+  item, `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`, where
+  `difference` is `actual - theoretical`, for items with use in those days.
