+## Sales
+
+- A sale is one till line: `ticket`, `soldAt` (instant), `dishId`, `qty`,
+  and `use`, the ingredient quantities it used (one recipe portion per dish
+  sold, fixed when it is imported). Sales live in `sales`.
+- A ticket is imported once; importing it again is skipped. Importing a file
+  is all or nothing. Its ingredients are consumed with `ref` `sale:<ticket>`
+  and `at` set to `soldAt`, one movement per batch per ticket.
+- Variance for a range of days: theoretical use is the `use` of sales sold in
+  those days; actual use is every `consume` movement in those days;
+  difference is actual minus theoretical.
